╭─ Issue description ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Issue Title: [Bug]: AnthropicChatFormatter splits parallel tool_results into multiple user messages -> 400 on DeepSeek                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Description:                                                                                                                                    │
│ ### Prerequisites                                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ -  I have searched the existing (https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/issues) and                                                        │
│ (https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/discussions), and this is not a duplicate.                                                         │
│ -  This is a bug, not a usage question. (For questions, please use                                                                              │
│ [Discussions](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/discussions/new?category=general) instead.)                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Background / Description                                                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Using agentscope with DeepSeek (Anthropic-compatible endpoint). When the model returns several tool_use blocks in one reply, the next call      │
│ fails with 400.                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ AnthropicChatFormatter splits the tool_results into multiple user messages, but they should be in ONE user message right after the assistant    │
│ message. DeepSeek checks this strictly and rejects it. Anthropic/GLM endpoints are lenient so it stays hidden.                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Root cause: in agentscope/formatter/_anthropic_formatter.py, the ToolResultBlock branch flushes whenever content_blocks is non-empty, so each   │
│ tool_result becomes its own user message. One-line fix works (see Steps to Reproduce).                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Error Messages                                                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```shell                                                                                                                                        │
│ anthropic.BadRequestError: 400 - {                                                                                                              │
│   'error': {                                                                                                                                    │
│     'message': "messages.7:`tool_use` ids were found without `tool_result` blocks immediately after: call_00_..., call_01_..., call_02_...,     │
│ call_04_.... Each `tool_use` block must have a corresponding `tool_result` block in the next message.",                                         │
│     'type': 'invalid_request_error'                                                                                                             │
│   }                                                                                                                                             │
│ }                                                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ messages.7 = assistant turn with 5 tool_use blocks. The 5 tool_results ran fine but were sent as separate user messages.                        │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Steps to Reproduce                                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Triggers when the model returns 2+ tool_use blocks in one reply. agentscope stores them + their tool_results in the same AssistantMsg.content:  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Run the formatter -> you get 1 assistant + 3 user messages (one per tool_result), instead of 1 assistant + 1 user. DeepSeek rejects it.         │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Setting tools to sequential (is_concurrency_safe=False) does NOT help — _save_to_context still merges all tool_results into one assistant       │
│ message.                                                                                                                                        │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Suggested fix in agentscope/formatter/_anthropic_formatter.py, ToolResultBlock branch:                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│   - if content_blocks:                                                                                                                          │
│   + if content_blocks and not has_tool_result:                                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ First tool_result still flushes the assistant content (unchanged); following tool_results then merge into one user message. Single-tool output  │
│ identical before/after.                                                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Environment                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ - AgentScope Version: 2.0.0                                                                                                                     │
│ - Python Version: 3.11                                                                                                                          │
│ - OS: macOS (darwin, arm64)                                                                                                                     │
│ - Model: DeepSeek deepseek-v4-pro via Anthropic-compatible endpoint                                                                             │
