│ split into separate user messages because of the flush             │
│ (messages.append) each time a ToolResultBlock is encountered and   │
│ content_blocks is non-empty. The flush happens unconditionally for │
│ every ToolResultBlock when content_blocks is not empty, causing    │
│ multiple user messages for multiple tool_results.                  │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
│ The intended behavior is to prevent flushing multiple times when   │
│ formatting sequential tool_results. The flush should happen once   │
│ before the first tool_result, but subsequent tool_results should   │
│ continue accumulating in content_blocks, avoiding creation of      │
│ multiple user messages.                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ Thus, the flush condition should be changed from:                  │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  if content_blocks:                                                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ to:                                                                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  if content_blocks and not has_tool_result:                        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Thereby, the first tool_result flushes existing content_blocks and │
│ sets has_tool_result True, subsequent tool_results skip the flush  │
│ and continue adding content to content_blocks, ultimately creating │
│ a single user message with all tool_results together.              │
│                                                                    │
│ This fix will ensure that multiple tool_results get merged into    │
│ one user message, preserving the strict message format required by │
│ DeepSeek.                                                          │
